From 7ce122d14c62bf3db225841e517dc2e47424076a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: LLCOOLT <114613597+LLCOOLT@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 20:50:34 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] display: picture effects and a capture of the presented
 picture

aurora_set_picture_effects (include/aurora/picture.h): a pass of its own over
the resampled present picture: a cut-paper outline or folding light, a colour
look (a 3x4 matrix), a vignette, depth of field round a focus point, and a
frame (a paper border, a stamp, a film strip, a storybook's). None: no pass.
aurora_capture_picture: the next presented picture as shown (after the
effects, at its presented size) read back once, as RGBA, to a callback.
In lib/webgpu/picture.cpp; its hooks kept apart from the earlier patches'
lines, so each of them still checks as applied.
---
